                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "14dbddc3-ca5e-4cfd-86a2-4d1e4cb9b4c7",
                        "source_entry_id": "d503428b-57ea-37ad-a99e-e1f7d4681ab8",
                        "source_sense_id": "c9658e2a-3405-3e6f-bc92-e4810bcab9f7",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Zoologie) Serpent",
                        "target_lang_word": "pit adder",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pit adder",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1303864-29ce-3ecd-a3d8-0d3001bfc794",
                                        "entry_id": "bacaa288-6187-3ef3-8819-966337565f2d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various venomous snakes of the family Crotalinae, found in Asia and the Americas, with a deep pit or groove on either side of the head which enables them to detect prey by infrared sensing; a pit viper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "939b93fe-a8db-47df-9f45-556139aaa924",
                                                "sense_id": "f1303864-29ce-3ecd-a3d8-0d3001bfc794",
                                                "text": "The two chief poisonous families of the rest of the globe, the vipers (Viperidae) and the pit-adders (Crotalida;), are entirely absent, their place being supplied by the Elapidae, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da5da30b-6115-4e26-b278-19592aa9deea",
                                                "sense_id": "f1303864-29ce-3ecd-a3d8-0d3001bfc794",
                                                "text": "The venom of some snakes, Rogers says, contains a mixture of the above-mentioned venoms (among such snakes are the Australian colubrines and the American pit-adders)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4849f38-8e5f-4aa5-a0a7-8e7cd111eba1",
                                                "sense_id": "f1303864-29ce-3ecd-a3d8-0d3001bfc794",
                                                "text": "There is the pit adder called Habu. This kind is the worst of the three. These snakes are three inches thick and six feet long, and resemble our diamond back rattlers at home."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68325e29-eb19-4e51-82f8-0775e1b50a82",
                                                "sense_id": "f1303864-29ce-3ecd-a3d8-0d3001bfc794",
                                                "text": "Goblins which surrounded you, crowding closer and closer with their eye stalks vibrating, goblins which hissed like pit adders, were perhaps something he had not reckoned with."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b474fd66-acbb-402b-8aba-c5a9549a1e6b",
                                                "sense_id": "f1303864-29ce-3ecd-a3d8-0d3001bfc794",
                                                "text": "They are neither lovable nor loving because they are innately poisonous or repulsive, like a pit adder or a skunk."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f44e4aa-aa9e-4538-bd9e-3427a10f0ed7",
                                                "sense_id": "f1303864-29ce-3ecd-a3d8-0d3001bfc794",
                                                "text": "\"[...] I hope the events of the day haven't so unbalanced your sense of values that you're going to turn on your pilot like a maddened pit adder at the mere suggestion of something pleasurable.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "958b626a-8618-47e7-8d05-4de1081cb82d",
                        "source_entry_id": "d503428b-57ea-37ad-a99e-e1f7d4681ab8",
                        "source_sense_id": "c9658e2a-3405-3e6f-bc92-e4810bcab9f7",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Zoologie) Serpent",
                        "target_lang_word": "rattlesnake",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rattlesnake",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b19f1c9a-f06d-3b31-b6f9-cdd5eb48b00d",
                                        "entry_id": "a48eadc5-b459-337a-81cb-1b454c101c98",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various venomous American snakes, of genera Crotalus and Sistrurus, having a rattle at the end of its tail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8675cad6-9d4a-4ecd-93c2-7076c6acdbc1",
                                                "sense_id": "b19f1c9a-f06d-3b31-b6f9-cdd5eb48b00d",
                                                "text": "Hooded rattlesnakes, horned toads, and lizards crawl in the dust and among the rocks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aec55761-e6fa-46f7-8092-1fbf2d64dc28",
                                                "sense_id": "b19f1c9a-f06d-3b31-b6f9-cdd5eb48b00d",
                                                "text": "The country ran shuttles and posted signs encouraging visitors to enjoy the display responsibly, but those precautions didn't prevent rattlesnake bites, twisted ankles, heat exhaustion, Instacelebs and other selfie-takers lying in or otherwise trampling the delicate blooms they'd come to see."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca52ad2c-ea69-4042-8620-622f3b409c9f",
                                                "sense_id": "b19f1c9a-f06d-3b31-b6f9-cdd5eb48b00d",
                                                "text": "Generally not aggressive, rattlesnakes strike when threatened or deliberately provoked, but given room they will retreat. Most snake bites occur when a rattlesnake is handled or accidentally touched by someone walking or climbing. The majority of snakebites occur on the hands, feet and ankles."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
